\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Controlled path count ($N=32$, $P=30$, SNR $=5$~dB, RSR $=12$~dB, $400$ trials per point, $L$ fixed and identical across users). (a) The two baselines are flat in $L$---path count does not affect an estimator that ignores structure---which confirms the sweep is not confounded; HS-GS rises to meet them. (b) The paired gain decays monotonically to zero as $L$ approaches the rank ceiling $r_{\max }=\lceil N/2\rceil =16$; the $95\%$ paired bootstrap band is plotted but is narrower than the markers. The hypothesis producing this figure was recorded before the experiment was run.}}{5}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:pathcount}{{3}{5}{}{}{}}
